ate: Question → What I will measure/ask → How I will record → How many trials/people → Graph I will use → What I will look for.\n\nTRY FIRST\nDraft a plan for: “Which vowel appears most in a page of a book?” List method and recording.\n\nFEEDBACK\nTally vowels on one page; table of A E I O U; column graph; look for tallest bar.","explain":"A Year 3 investigation plan states a question, the data or experiment method, how results will be recorded and what “finished” looks like.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS\nThis helps the learner choose methods based on place value, quantity and accurate working, rather than guessing digits by shape alone. Keep every step justified.\n\nHOW TO WORK\nRead the worked example and name the places, values or distances that carry the method. Before looking at the correction, make your own attempt using the exact question provided. Compare your working with the feedback: did you use the same skill and show your reasoning? If a digit or place is uncertain, identify what would have to be regrouped or counted again. One deliberate, justified revision is more useful than writing a longer answer.","icon":"📖","notice":"Starting without a question wastes trials that do not answer anything. Correct the value or method, not just the appearance of the digits.","title":"Understand and model","visual":[{"alt":"Investigation planning template.","caption":"No question → wasted trials.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#297a61\"/><g font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#263948\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\">Plan</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\">question → method → record</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"42\">Then</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"78\">graph → look for</text></g></svg>"}],"visual_before":[{"episode":{"scenes":[{"bg":"room","lines":[{"text":"I can see the example, but I am not sure which number or place matters most.","who":"pip"},{"text":"Name the places, values or distances that carry the method before you decide.","who":"juno"},{"text":"I will try the prompt myself, then compare with the feedback.","who":"pip"},{"pause_after":true,"text":"Pause here. Use this model: Plan template: Question → What I will measure/ask → How I will record → How many trials/people → Graph I will use → What Then write your own working.","who":"juno"}]}],"title":"Talk through the first model","transcript":"Pip: I can see the example, but I am not sure which number or place matters most.\nJuno: Name the places, values or distances that carry the method before you decide.\nPip: I will try the prompt myself, then compare with the feedback.\nJuno: Pause here. Use this model: Plan template: Question → What I will measure/ask → How I will record → How many trials/people → Graph I will use → What Then write your own working."}}]},{"check":{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Make the method visible: name the values, places or steps you used and say why that step is valid. Supported working follows the actual numbers and purpose of the task.","options":["Make the method visible: name the values, places or steps you used and say why that step is valid.","A calculation unrelated to the numbers given.","An answer copied without understanding.","A guess with no working."],"question":"What should you demonstrate in this teaching stage?"},"example":"WORKED MODEL\nPlan template: Question → What I will measure/ask → How I will record → How many trials/people → Graph I will use → What I will look for. Look at each number, place or distance that carries the method.\n\nTRY FIRST\nWrite the key numbers from the model and say what each one represents in the method.\n\nFEEDBACK\nThe most useful working names the quantities and the reason for each step, not only the final answer.","explain":"Make the method visible: name the values, places or steps you used and say why 