ing stage?"},"example":"WORKED MODEL\nStarting without a question wastes trials that do not answer anything. Here is a more productive model: Plan template: Question → What I will measure/ask → How I will record → How many trials/people → Graph I will use → What I will look for.\n\nTRY FIRST\nDescribe why the warned-against approach gives the wrong value or meaning, then write corrected working.\n\nFEEDBACK\nTally vowels on one page; table of A E I O U; column graph; look for tallest bar.","explain":"Use an intentionally incorrect attempt as a comparison. Name its specific mathematical error, then show the corrected working.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS\nThis helps the learner choose methods based on place value, quantity and accurate working, rather than guessing digits by shape alone. Keep every step justified.\n\nHOW TO WORK\nRead the worked example and name the places, values or distances that carry the method. Before looking at the correction, make your own attempt using the exact question provided. Compare your working with the feedback: did you use the same skill and show your reasoning? If a digit or place is uncertain, identify what would have to be regrouped or counted again. One deliberate, justified revision is more useful than writing a longer answer.","icon":"📖","notice":"Changing the answer without repairing the method does not fix the error. Starting without a question wastes trials that do not answer anything. Correct the value or method, not just the appearance of the digits.","title":"Test a misconception"},{"check":{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Use the method on new numbers or a new context, not a copy of the worked example. Review accuracy and units or places. Supported working follows the actual numbers and purpose of the task.","options":["Use the method on new numbers or a new context, not a copy of the worked example. Review accuracy and units or places.","A calculation unrelated to the numbers given.","An answer copied without understanding.","A g